    "description": "Lumber camp (sawmill), level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. A miniature sawmill: logs from the front yard (log pile, crane with a hanging log) ride a carriage line of stripped logs into an open-sided timber shed under a lean-to roof, through the saw (grindstone, the workstation; a stonecutter joins at L2) and out to the plank yard behind. L2 adds a waterwheel in a stone race driving the saw, plank stacks, sawhorse, sawdust, lanterns, a sign; L3 an axe in the chopping block, saplings, moss. Not yet builder-tested: stonecutter. Decoration step adds: sign_text, water.",
    "changes": "Rebuilt as a proper sawmill you can read at a glance: an open timber shed with the saw on a log-carriage line, a log pile and crane in front, plank stacks behind, and from L2 a waterwheel driving the saw.",
